## the probe fixes, and that they do not change what the probes do

a189 cleanup body, as it was: for pid in "${started[@]:-}";  do kill -TERM "$pid" 2>/dev/null;  done; [ -n "${RUN_DIR:-}" ] && rm -rf "$RUN_DIR"
a189 trap body, as it is    : for pid in "${started[@]:-}"; do kill -TERM "$pid" 2>/dev/null; done; [ -n "${RUN_DIR:-}" ] && rm -rf "$RUN_DIR"
the same two commands in the same order; the only difference is the space after the ';' that
separates them now that they share one trap string

